Some useful functions from other the other mods bundled with this that may be useful to be aware of.

VCOMAI:
	(group this) setVariable ["VCM_NOFLANK",true]; //This command will stop the AI squad from executing advanced movement maneuvers.
	(group this) setVariable ["VCM_NORESCUE",true]; //This command will stop the AI squad from responding to calls for backup.
	(group this) setVariable ["VCM_TOUGHSQUAD",true]; //This command will stop the AI squad from calling for backup.
	(group this) setVariable ["Vcm_Disable",true]; //This command will disable Vcom AI on a group entirely.
	(group this) setVariable ["VCM_DisableForm",true]; //This command will disable AI group from changing formations.	
	(group this) setVariable ["VCM_Skilldisable",true]; //This command will disable an AI group from being impacted by Vcom AI skill changes.

LambsFSM (from GitHub Wiki):
	setVariables:
		Main:
			<group> setVariable ["lambs_danger_disableGroupAI", true]; - Disables certain LAMBS features, such as coordinating assults with other groups, ambushing vehicles, ect.
			<unit> setVariable ["lambs_danger_disableAI", true]; - Self explanitory, will prevent AI from intentially entering and clearing buildings
			<group> setVariable ["lambs_danger_dangerFormation", "FILE"]; - Formation group will attempt to switch to on first contact. (Useful for Ex: CQC units closing distance)
			<unit> setVariable ["lambs_danger_dangerRadio", true]; - If group contains unit with radio variable, increases there reporting range,frequency, and accuracy according to settings
			<group> setVariable ["lambs_danger_enableGroupReinforce", true, true] - Groups with the reinforcement variable set will respond to friendly information sharing events.
				Possible Responses Include:
					- Change formation and move towards or reposition group members according to threat type and group's equipment
					- Fire Flares towards known threat direction
					- Reposition/Move static weapons via dismentaling/assembling
					- Change group formation according to threat type
					(Should not interfere with other mods or scripted AI orders)
		Info:
			<group> getVariable "lambs_danger_isExecutingTactic"
			<group> getVariable "lambs_danger_contact"
		Debug/Testing:
			<unit> getVariable "lambs_main_FSMDangerCauseData" - Checking this variable will give the current FSM data that the AI is responding to.
			<unit> getVariable "lambs_main_currentTarget"
			<unit> getVariable "lambs_main_currentTask"
			<group> getVariable "lambs_main_currentTactic"
	
	AI scripted commands:
		*Note "Area" refers to an array of: [sizeX, sizeY, angle, isRectangle, sizeZ]
		taskArtillery: 
			- [ArtillaryUnit, targetPos, strikeCaller, roundsToFire, accuracy(int: 0-100), requiresAmmo (boolean)] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskArtillery;
			- Preforms artillary strike at given position
		taskArtilleryRegister: 
			- [artillaryUnitOrGroup] call lambs_wp_fnc_taskArtilleryRegister;
			- Registers unit as an artillary peices for artillary support requests
		taskAssault:
			- [unitToDoCharge, destinationPos, IsForcedRetreat, distanceThreshold, updateCycle, isCalledForWaypoint] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskAssault;
			- Causes AI to wrecklessly charge a given positoin, with optional retreat parameters
		taskCamp:
			- [group, centerOfCamp, rangeToSendPatrols, campArea, canTeleportUnitsToPos, allowPartialPatrols] call lambs_wp_fnc_taskCamp;
			- Improved (aka built for lambs) version of CBA_fnc_taskDefend
		taskCQB:
			- [group, centerPos, range, cycleDelay, campArea, doCalledForWaypoints] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskCQB;
			- Assigned Group will apply logic to search and clear all buildings in a radius
		taskGarrison:
			- [group, garrisonCenter, radius, campArea, doTeleportUnits, sortBasedOffHeight, conditionToFreeUnit, doSubGroupsPatrol] call lambs_wp_fnc_taskGarrison;
			- The AI will occupy buildings and man static weapons in area, will remain in place until a freeing condition is met
			- conditions are (-2 Random, -1 All, 0 None, 1 Hit, 2 Fired, 3 FiredNear, 4 Suppressed),
		taskPatrol:
			- [group, position, radius, maxWaypoints, campArea, doDynamicPatrolPatterns] call lambs_wp_fnc_taskPatrol;
			- Simple dynamic patrol script, only for infantry
		taskReset
			- [group] call lambs_wp_fnc_taskReset;
			- Correctly stops any assigned lambs tasks for a group
		taskRush
			- [group, maxRange, cyclesDelay, campArea, centerPos, doOnlyHuntPlayers] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskRush;
			- AI will aggresivly hunt closest group with perfect knowledge, but will not begin firing without having seen target
		taskHunt
			- [group, maxRange, cyclesDelay, campArea, centerPos, doOnlyPlayers, doDynamicReinforcement, flareSetting] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskHunt;
			- AI will patrol an area around the closest target which gradually grows smaller around target.
			- Flare options include: 0 disabled, 1 enabled (if Units cant fire it them self a flare is created via createVehicle), 2 Only if Units can Fire UGL them self
		taskCreep
			- [group, maxRange, cyclesDelay, campArea, centerPos, doOnlyPlayers] spawn lambs_wp_fnc_taskCreep;
			- AI uses cover to attempt to get as close to the nearest target as possible before opening fire.
			
	Global Variables:
		disableAIGestures(boolean)
			- Toggles unit gestures and hand signals when reacting to danger or executing planned manoeuvres
		disableAICallouts(boolean)
			- Toggles extra unit callouts based on situations
		disableAIDodge(boolean)
			- Toggles unit quickly dodging or changing stance in response to being hit.\nImmediate reactions force an animation to run. Disabling will make for a more static AI
		disableAIFleeing(boolean)
			- Toggles enhanced fleeing function for units.
		indoorMove(0 - 1, inc 0.1, 2)
			- Indoor Move Chance
		disableAutonomousMunitionSwitching(boolean)
			- When unchecked allows the vehicle to autonomously switch munition type in favor against the current target. E.g., AP against armored targets, HE against unarmored ones
		disablePlayerGroupSuppression(boolean)
			- Toggle autonomous suppression for units in player group
		minSuppressionRange(1-500, inc 50, 0)
			- If the target or a blocking obstacle is within this distance, the AI will not perform suppression fire
		minFriendlySuppressionDistance(0 - 50, inc 5, 0)
			- If there are allies within this distance, AI will not perform suppression fire. Set to 0 to disable.
		minObstacleProximity(0-20, inc 5, 2)
			- Minimum Obstacle Proximity Distance for Suppressive Fire
		radioDisabled(boolean)
			- Toggle information sharing between units
		maxRevealValue(0-4, inc 1, 2)
			- Maximum 'knowsAbout' value shared between groups. Setting greater than 1 may cause distant allies to go into full danger mode.
		combatShareRange(0-1000, inc 200, 0)
			- Friendly groups within range will be set to combat behaviour. Units in combat mode will seek cover and concealment and turn towards nearest known threat.
		radioShout(20-200, inc 100, 0)
			- Range AI units share information without radios
		radioWest(20-3000, inc 500, 0)
			- Base range side WEST share information
		radioEast(20-3000, inc 500, 0)
			- Base range side EAST share information
		radioGuer(20-3000, inc 500, 0)
			- Base range side GUER share information
		radioBackpack(500-6000, inc 2000, 0)
			- Units equipped with backpack radios (vanilla, TFAR, or configured by variable) add this value to the base information sharing range
		debug_FSM(boolean)
			- Shows FSM debug messages

